<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Banco Frances raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Banco Frances raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley Dean Witter analysts Rafael Bello and Yovanka Bylander raised their rating for Argentina's Banco Frances to outperform from underperform.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Two catalysts are likely to take the stock to higher levels, in our view -- a benign U.S. interest rate environment and very strong growth in the Argentine economy,&quot; they wrote in a report.</p>
<p>-- They set a price target of $41 per American Depositary Receipt.  Closed Wednesday at 34-14/16 in New York.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk (212) 859-1730))</p>
